attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 1, `rbbA` to `yhhJ`, are carried by 97 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 99.6 to 99.8% of them, fewest at column 1, `yhhJ`, 99.6% {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `yhhI`**, column 2, carried by 43%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2.c2, P}. Then the `nik` genes, columns 4 to 9, [[nickel import and transport]], carried by 96 to 97% {S3, Q}. Through columns 57 to 59 a branch of 3 shell families runs in 15 to 36%, [[phosphate transport]] {S8.b57}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 91%, and hesitates less there, 0.14 against 0.26 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 2, `yhhI`, a fork column, 1.15 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in fork and variable columns.** Columns 57 to 79 are carried by 36 to 89% of chromosomes, 22 persistent and 1 shell {S8}. The last column is `pckA`, in 36% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.18 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.52 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 82% against 94% {C}.

